+## 53.4 (Tremendously Improved) AI overbuilding very cheap combat units (ancient macemen only being an issue as of now anyways etc) in the early game, sometimes even at turn 100, which is inefficient and easy to overshoot if i may say but anyways etc, as they are cheap and accumulate quickly, but are not too effective especially as soon as we get archer units anyways etc, now limited, especially even more so after as of now turn 50 where they should be especially useless; much better military compositions and better growth as a result anyways etc
+
+See screenshots and files about/related(ing? Anyways etc) to this issue in this [google drive folder link](https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1NDQ2qC5wr7f3ERVIxzE9HzyYs5hnW89e?usp=sharing)
+
+This is another very nice change, that should make AI significantly stronger and more efficient with its unit compositions anyways etc.
+
+I have noticed AI produce ancient macemen if left unchecked even at turn 100 which is especially useless, and as they are so cheap they tend to quickly pile up.
+
+In our mod, ancient macemen have more strength than archers but are worse at city combat (plus archers are available very early at as of now tech_hunting, so some civs even start with them directly anyways etc, and so i mean but anyways etc we should really avoid overstacking ancient macemen after our minimal offense or such very early needs if i am not mistaken in my thinking which i think i am not and based on results below too if i may say but anyways etc but check to be sure i mean if i may say but anyways etc), so after the very early game they are mostly useless, plus archers are more versatile and help us fill our defensive quotas so better choice long term anyways etc. And since archers are more expensive, we will build less so will go bankrupt not as soon, spend less time upgrading ancient macemen but instead directly build axemen or swordsmen or such, at least seems so in autoplay anyways etc. So we now make it even stricter after turn as of now 50 adjusted to game speed but anyways etc.
+
+As compared to before changes (see screenshots in known issue [53.2.2 (Seemingly greatly enhanced) AI overproducing defenders early on, especially longbowmen but not only, replaced with an early produce more versatile units especially civ-specific ones when defended enough (at least in theory anyways etc) in CvCityAI::AI_chooseUnit anyways etc](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs_And_Appendixes/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#5322-seemingly-greatly-enhanced-ai-overproducing-defenders-early-on-especially-longbowmen-but-not-only-replaced-with-an-early-produce-more-versatile-units-especially-civ-specific-ones-when-defended-enough-at-least-in-theory-anyways-etc-in-cvcityaiai_chooseunit-anyways-etc) for comparison, including the cfc forum link there for the other map's compositions) in `CvCityAI::AI_chooseUnit` to fix this very cheap combat units being produced issue but anyways etc, we have now much less ancient macemen at turn +/- 100, and more stronger units like swordsmen or such in composition of AI players, which seems very sane, more efficient economically and militarily if i may say but anyways etc, and very strong too at least significantly stronger it seems (e.g. 3 vs 11 ancient macemen at turns 100-130 for example from what i remember of it anyways etc) but anyways etc.
+
+Note: the way the code is as of now written but anyways etc, it may apply to scouts as well since they have strength/combat as well if i'm not mistaken, but the cap should be large enough that it shouldn't be a concern (unless we overproduce them then fine to limit them as well if i'm not mistaken but anyways etc).
+
